  volume = {34},
  number = {14},
  pages  = {25823-25833},
  year   = {2026},
  doi    = {10.1364/OE.601412},
  eprint = {2604.19311},
  archivePrefix= {arXiv},
  note   = {PDF\_papers/Ko\_2026\_Rydberg-fluorescence-mmWave-electric-field-imaging-Autler-Townes.pdf.
             Warsaw (Ko, Krokosz, Mazelanik, Wasilewski, Parniak): images
             millimetre-wave electric fields inside a warm 87Rb vapour
             cell via a 3-photon optical ladder (780+776+1269 nm) to a
             Rydberg F-state, then reads the mmWave-driven Autler-Townes
             splitting of the fluorescence spectrum against a 34D5/2
             Rydberg resonance for absolute field calibration, fit with a
             steady-state GKSL master equation. Different transition
             ladder, different mechanism (Rydberg-Rydberg mmWave coupling
             and RF electrometry, not an S-S two-photon AC-Stark
             asymmetric lineshape), no self-broadening or polarizability
             number in common. No physics bridge. The
             velocity-class-weighted steady-state density matrix with an
             added transit decay rate is methodologically familiar, not a
             numeric or physics transfer. Lineage placement stands
             separately: camera-imaged, position-resolved reconstruction
             of a field amplitude Omega_mm(z) along the beam via AT
             splitting, the where-along-the-beam sibling of patrick2025's
             where and this repository's own shape (see BRIDGES section
             below). The 11th page (references 21-32) carries no visible
             running header in the held file, unlike every other page.
             Pages 25823-25833 assumes 11 sequential pages from the stated
             first page 25823. VERIFY the closing page number at
             submission.. arXiv 2604.19311 has two versions, v1 21 Apr
             2026 and v2 7 Jul 2026. The v2 title, confirmed against the
             arXiv abstract page, matches the published title verbatim.
             The v1 title was NOT independently confirmed from the
             abstract page itself, only from a search-engine snippet that
             showed a shorter form without "Background-free", so treat any
             v1-title claim as unverified..}
}

